{"id": "BT-0046", "category": "coding", "issue": "A laptop costing $2,635.45 ex GST is above the $1,000 capitalise threshold and lasts more than a year, but it was expensed to Repairs and Maintenance.", "proposed_fix": "Recode the line from 473 Repairs and Maintenance to 720 Computer Equipment (fixed asset) at $2,635.45 ex GST, and add it to the fixed asset register for depreciation. The tax treatment is for the GST reviewer to check.", "evidence": "BT-0046, 2026-08-16, Contact JB Hi-Fi Business (default account 720), Description \"Laptop for estimator\", AccountCode 473, TaxType INPUT, LineAmount 2635.45, TaxAmount 263.55, Total 2899.00. Organisation Policies.CapitaliseThreshold 1000.0.", "confidence": "high", "queued_at": "2026-09-29T13:02:47"}
{"id": "BT-0047", "category": "coding", "issue": "A joinery install charge from a subcontractor was coded to Materials instead of Subcontractors, which distorts job costing for J-118.", "proposed_fix": "Recode the line from 310 Materials to 315 Subcontractors at $5,800.00 ex GST (Total $6,380.00), keeping job J-118. If the invoice shows a separate materials component, split that part to 310.", "evidence": "BT-0047, 2026-08-22, Contact Pinewood Joinery (default account 315; its other payments BT-0030, BT-0031 and BT-0033 are progress claims coded 315), Description \"Joinery install, job J-118\", AccountCode 310, TaxType INPUT, LineAmount 5800.00, TaxAmount 580.00, Total 6380.00.", "confidence": "high", "queued_at": "2026-09-29T13:02:50"}
{"id": "BT-0052", "category": "recon", "issue": "BT-0052 totals $1,254.00, but the bank statement line it is matched to (SL-0051) shows $1,524.00 paid. The $270.00 gap looks like transposed digits.", "proposed_fix": "Check the Coastal Electrical Contractors tax invoice for the J-124 progress claim. If the invoice is $1,524.00 (the amount that left the bank), correct BT-0052 to Total 1524.00: LineAmount 1385.45, TaxAmount 138.55 (1524.00 / 11), account 315. If the invoice really is $1,254.00, the extra $270.00 is an overpayment. Ask the supplier for a credit or refund and record the $270.00 as a receivable from them.", "evidence": "SL-0051: Date 2026-08-24, Payee COASTAL ELECTRICAL CON, Amount -1524.00, MatchedTransactionID BT-0052. BT-0052: Contact Coastal Electrical Contractors, Date 2026-08-24, \"Progress claim, job J-124\", account 315, TaxType INPUT, LineAmount 1140.00, TaxAmount 114.00, Total 1254.00, IsReconciled true. The difference is 270.00, which divides by 9, the usual sign of a transposition (1524 vs 1254).", "confidence": "high", "queued_at": "2026-09-29T13:02:51"}
{"id": "BT-0048", "category": "coding", "issue": "A Woolworths grocery purchase on the company account was coded to Entertainment and looks like private spending.", "proposed_fix": "Ask the client whether this had a business purpose. If it was private, recode the full $214.35 to 880 Owner A Drawings as BAS Excluded with no GST. The GST reversal is a separate GST finding.", "evidence": "BT-0048, 2026-08-23, Contact Woolworths, Description \"Groceries\", AccountCode 420 Entertainment, TaxType INPUT, LineAmount 194.86, TaxAmount 19.49, Total 214.35.", "confidence": "medium", "queued_at": "2026-09-29T13:02:53"}
{"id": "SL-0052", "category": "recon", "issue": "The $8,420.00 ATO payment on 28 Aug 2026 (SL-0052) has no Xero transaction, so it is missing from the books.", "proposed_fix": "This is most likely a payment of a prior-period BAS/IAS liability (GST and PAYG withholding) to the ATO integrated client account. Once confirmed, record a spend money transaction of $8,420.00 to ATO, dated 2026-08-28. Code it against the GST and PAYG Withholding liability accounts (or an ATO ICA clearing account) with TaxType BAS Excluded, then reconcile it to SL-0052. To confirm, ask the client for the ATO integrated client account statement and the lodged BAS/IAS showing $8,420.00 payable, and check whether it includes any GIC or penalties, which would go to an expense account.", "evidence": "SL-0052: Date 2026-08-28, Payee ATO PAYMENT, Amount -8420.00, MatchedTransactionID null. No bank transaction for ATO appears in the list of 52 transactions (BT-0001 to BT-0052).", "confidence": "medium", "queued_at": "2026-09-29T13:02:55"}
{"id": "BT-0049", "category": "coding", "issue": "A 12-month insurance premium (to 31 Jul 2027) was expensed in full to Insurance in August instead of going to Prepayments and being released monthly.", "proposed_fix": "Recode the $4,800.00 ex GST to 620 Prepayments and keep the $480.00 GST credit. Release $400.00 a month ($4,800.00 / 12) to 433 Insurance, starting August 2026. That leaves $400.00 in Insurance for August and $4,400.00 in Prepayments at 31 Aug 2026.", "evidence": "BT-0049, 2026-08-02, Contact QBE Insurance, Description \"Contract works insurance, 12 months to 31 Jul 2027\", AccountCode 433, TaxType INPUT, LineAmount 4800.00, TaxAmount 480.00, Total 5280.00. Period 2026-08-01 to 2026-08-31; CapitaliseThreshold 1000.0.", "confidence": "high", "queued_at": "2026-09-29T13:02:56"}
{"id": "BT-0043", "category": "gst", "issue": "A GST credit of $360.00 was claimed on a payment to Ridge Tiling, a sole trader who is not registered for GST.", "proposed_fix": "Change TaxType from INPUT to GST free (no credit): LineAmount 3,960.00, TaxAmount 0.00. The GST credit claimed drops by $360.00. Keep account 315.", "evidence": "BT-0043, 2026-08-26, Contact 'Ridge Tiling (sole trader)', 'Tiling, job J-121', AccountCode 315, TaxType INPUT, LineAmount 3600.00, TaxAmount 360.00, Total 3960.00. Contact C006 IsGSTRegistered false (ABN 71 824 330 016).", "confidence": "high", "queued_at": "2026-09-29T13:02:57"}
{"id": "BT-0044", "category": "gst", "issue": "Casual wages were coded INPUT and claimed a $300.00 GST credit, but wages are BAS Excluded.", "proposed_fix": "Change TaxType to BASEXCLUDED: LineAmount 3,300.00, TaxAmount 0.00 on account 477. The GST credit claimed drops by $300.00.", "evidence": "BT-0044, 2026-08-17, Contact 'Payroll Clearing', 'Weekly wages (casual)', AccountCode 477 (Wages and Salaries, default BASEXCLUDED), TaxType INPUT, LineAmount 3000.00, TaxAmount 300.00, Total 3300.00. Contact C020 IsGSTRegistered false. The other wage runs (BT-0001 to BT-0005) are BASEXCLUDED.", "confidence": "high", "queued_at": "2026-09-29T13:03:00"}
{"id": "BT-0045", "category": "gst", "issue": "GST was worked out as 10% of the total ($217.80) instead of 1/11 of the total ($198.00), so the credit is overstated by $19.80.", "proposed_fix": "Correct TaxAmount to 198.00 (2,178.00 / 11) and LineAmount to 1,980.00. The Total stays at 2,178.00.", "evidence": "BT-0045, 2026-08-09, Contact 'Laminex Direct', 'Benchtop laminate, job J-124', AccountCode 310, TaxType INPUT, LineAmount 1960.20, TaxAmount 217.80, Total 2178.00. 2178.00 / 11 = 198.00; 2178.00 x 10% = 217.80.", "confidence": "high", "queued_at": "2026-09-29T13:03:03"}
{"id": "BT-0042", "category": "gst", "issue": "A merchant facility fee coded to Bank Fees claimed a $5.90 GST credit, but under firm policy bank fees are input taxed and get no GST credit.", "proposed_fix": "Change TaxType from INPUT to the account default EXEMPTEXPENSES (the same as the BT-0041 account keeping fee): LineAmount 64.90, TaxAmount 0.00. The GST credit drops by $5.90. Client question: does the CBA merchant statement show GST on this fee? If it is a valid tax invoice with GST, the reviewer may keep the credit.", "evidence": "BT-0042, 2026-08-31, Contact 'Commonwealth Bank', 'Merchant facility fee', AccountCode 404 (Bank Fees, default EXEMPTEXPENSES), TaxType INPUT, LineAmount 59.00, TaxAmount 5.90, Total 64.90. SKILL.md GST rule: 'Bank fees are input taxed: no GST credit.'", "confidence": "medium", "queued_at": "2026-09-29T13:03:07"}
{"id": "BT-0048", "category": "gst", "issue": "A $19.49 GST credit was claimed on Woolworths groceries, which look like private spending with no business purpose.", "proposed_fix": "Reverse the credit by setting TaxType to BASEXCLUDED with LineAmount 214.35 and TaxAmount 0.00. If confirmed private, recode to Owner A Drawings (880); that recode belongs to the coding reviewer. Client question: were these groceries for a business purpose (for example, a job site or staff amenities)?", "evidence": "BT-0048, 2026-08-23, Contact 'Woolworths', 'Groceries', AccountCode 420 (Entertainment), TaxType INPUT, LineAmount 194.86, TaxAmount 19.49, Total 214.35.", "confidence": "medium", "queued_at": "2026-09-29T13:03:10"}
